{"schema_version":1,"dataset_id":"metro-route-candidates","country":"LK","source_ids":["metro-coverage","lk-metro","osm-walk-colombo","lk-census-2024","gig-data-gnd-boundaries","osm","overture-places"],"vintage":"Walk graph 2026-10 · Census 2024 · CM stops 2026-08 · Overture 2026-09-23.1","title":"Illustrative Metro Bus route candidates","description":"Rule-generated links and extensions from existing Colombo Metro Bus stops into dense unserved neighbourhoods, scored on the residents, offices, schools and hospitals they would add.","grain":"One row per illustrative candidate route.","notes":["Derived by developing-country.org with scripts/build-metro-alternatives.mjs on the same model as the metro coverage tables: 80 m/min walking on the OpenStreetMap foot network (5 min = 400 m, 10 min = 800 m), reached streets buffered 50 m, a 5 m equal-area raster, Census 2024 GN population spread evenly within each division, Overture Maps office listings and OSM schools and hospitals.","Rule: for each gap cluster, largest unserved first, a link follows OSM main roads (trunk to tertiary) from the nearest existing interchange stop (2+ CM routes) to the cluster label point; an extension does the same from the nearest CM line terminus when it is a different stop within 10 km by road. At most 10 candidates are kept.","New stops are placed every 1006 m along the route — the median straight-line distance between consecutive CM stops in lk_metro order (148 gaps; the OSRM line geometry runs 25–50% longer than published route lengths, so it is not used) — and the last at the cluster label point.","Scores are marginal over the existing network: residents in walkshed cells no existing stop reaches, and offices, schools and hospitals newly within a 10-minute walk. Candidates may overlap each other; metro-route-scenarios accounts for that overlap."],"caveats":["Coverage-only analysis: no travel demand, origin–destination data, road capacity, bus operations, terminal space or cost is considered.","Population is spread evenly within each GN division; residents only, no workplace or daytime population; offices are listings, not jobs.","OSM street and path completeness limits every walkshed; candidate routes follow mapped main roads only.","Candidates are illustrative, generated by a mechanical rule; they are not recommendations or planned routes."],"primary_key":["candidate_id"],"fields":[{"id":"candidate_id","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Candidate ID"},{"id":"name","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Candidate"},{"id":"kind","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Kind (link or extension)"},{"id":"serves_cluster","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Gap clusters served"},{"id":"from_stop","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Existing stop"},{"id":"to_stop","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Gap cluster reached"},{"id":"length_km","role":"measure","type":"number","label":"Route length","unit":"km","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"stop_count","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"New stops","unit":"stops","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"new_pop_5min","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"New residents within a 5-minute walk","unit":"people","aggregation":"none"},{"id":"new_pop_10min","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"New residents within a 10-minute walk","unit":"people","aggregation":"none"},{"id":"new_offices_10min","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"New offices within a 10-minute walk","unit":"offices","aggregation":"none"},{"id":"new_schools_10min","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"New schools within a 10-minute walk","unit":"schools","aggregation":"none"},{"id":"new_hospitals_10min","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"New hospitals within a 10-minute walk","unit":"hospitals","aggregation":"none"},{"id":"new_pop_per_km","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"New residents within 10 minutes per route km","unit":"people per km","aggregation":"none"},{"id":"new_share_pct","role":"measure","type":"number","label":"New residents as a share of the study area","unit":"%","aggregation":"none"},{"id":"rank_new_pop_per_km","role":"dimension","type":"integer","label":"Rank by new residents per km"},{"id":"in_best_3","role":"dimension","type":"boolean","label":"In the best-3 scenario"},{"id":"color","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Map colour"}],"rows":[{"candidate_id":"cand-01","name":"Modara–Orugodawatta link","kind":"link","serves_cluster":"gap-01","from_stop":"Orugodawatta","to_stop":"Colombo (Modara–Mattakkuliya)","length_km":2.76,"stop_count":3,"new_pop_5min":7344,"new_pop_10min":14690,"new_offices_10min":6,"new_schools_10min":3,"new_hospitals_10min":0,"new_pop_per_km":5313,"new_share_pct":0.57,"rank_new_pop_per_km":4,"in_best_3":false,"color":"#e11d48"},{"candidate_id":"cand-02","name":"CM04 extension from Dematagoda to Modara","kind":"extension","serves_cluster":"gap-01","from_stop":"Dematagoda","to_stop":"Colombo (Modara–Mattakkuliya)","length_km":3.69,"stop_count":4,"new_pop_5min":16212,"new_pop_10min":40030,"new_offices_10min":40,"new_schools_10min":6,"new_hospitals_10min":0,"new_pop_per_km":10839,"new_share_pct":1.55,"rank_new_pop_per_km":1,"in_best_3":true,"color":"#0891b2"},{"candidate_id":"cand-03","name":"Megoda Kolonnawa–Dematagoda link","kind":"link","serves_cluster":"gap-02","from_stop":"Dematagoda","to_stop":"Kolonnawa (Megoda Kolonnawa–Wennawatta)","length_km":2.46,"stop_count":2,"new_pop_5min":4241,"new_pop_10min":16613,"new_offices_10min":13,"new_schools_10min":0,"new_hospitals_10min":1,"new_pop_per_km":6740,"new_share_pct":0.64,"rank_new_pop_per_km":2,"in_best_3":true,"color":"#65a30d"},{"candidate_id":"cand-04","name":"Pelenwatta West–Pannipitiya R.way link","kind":"link","serves_cluster":"gap-03","from_stop":"Pannipitiya R.way","to_stop":"Kesbewa (Pelenwatta West–Erewwala West)","length_km":4.02,"stop_count":4,"new_pop_5min":3581,"new_pop_10min":10459,"new_offices_10min":5,"new_schools_10min":4,"new_hosp